     kkyyuuaa ccoonnffiigg — Inspects the values of the loaded configuration

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     kkyyuuaa ccoonnffiigg [_v_a_r_i_a_b_l_e_1 _._. _v_a_r_i_a_b_l_e_N]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kkyyuuaa ccoonnffiigg command provides a way to list all defined configuration
     variables and their current values.

     This command is intended to help you in resolving the values of the con‐
     figuration variables without having to scan over configuration files.

     In the default synopsis form (no arguments), the command prints all con‐
     figuration variables.  If any arguments are provided, the command will
     only print the requested variables.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The kkyyuuaa ccoonnffiigg command returns 0 on success or 1 if any of the specified
     configuration variables does not exist.

     Additional exit codes may be returned as described in kyua(1).

